    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d46">

                <pb facs="0056" n="44" sameAs="frus:frus1940v05/pg44"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">810.20 Defense/58<hi rendition="#superscript"
                        >4/6</hi>: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Brazil</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Caffery</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Rio de
                                Janerio</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1940-06-04T11:00:00-03:00">June 4, 1940—11
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received 12:55 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>245. For the Under Secretary. My 235, May 29, 4 p.m. Aranha now says he is
                    disposed to cooperate with us in regard to our plans for security, et cetera,
                    for the Argentine and Uruguay. However, he still desires conversations regarding
                    the United States and Brazil military-naval understanding to be held
                    previously.</p>
                <pb facs="0057" n="45" xml:id="pg45"/>
                <p>He tells me that he hears from his Embassy at Buenos Aires that Chile has
                    suggested to the Argentine a military-naval understanding for Chile, Argentina
                    and Brazil.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Caffery</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
